### Code interpreter bots. Run demo.http steps 1-2 first (sign in, get a token).
### Prerequisite: the model in CODE_EMBEDDING_MODEL must be pulled in Ollama
###   (e.g. `ollama pull qwen3-embedding:4b`); it is registered automatically on startup.
@token = {{token}}
@botId = bot_REPLACE_ME

### 1. Create a code interpreter bot. Creates its own tables; the embedding dimension is
###    measured from the model. Returns 400 naming the model if it is not pulled/registered.
POST http://localhost:3000/bots
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "botName": "Shop code",
    "botDesc": "Explains the shop codebase",
    "botType": "Code_Interpreter",
    "owner": "shubhambankar65@gmail.com"
}

### 2. Chatting with a code bot through the KB endpoint is rejected (400) — use /code/:botId/chat (Phase 6).
POST http://localhost:3000/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "botId": "{{botId}}",
    "question": "hello"
}

### 3. Upload a zip of a repository (multipart). Returns 202 { runId, repoName } immediately;
###    indexing runs in the background. Fields: file (required, .zip), name (optional, defaults to
###    the file name), summarize (optional, "true" = also generate LLM summaries; slow).
###    Uploading the same name again re-indexes it and only re-embeds what changed.
###    409 if a run is already in progress for this bot.
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/repos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----code

------code
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

shop
------code
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="shop.zip"
Content-Type: application/zip

< ./shop.zip
------code--

### 4. Index a directory that is already on the server. Only works when CODE_REPOS_ROOT is set,
###    and the path must be inside it (relative to it, or absolute).
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/repos/path
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "path": "shop",
    "name": "shop"
}

### 5. Follow progress. The latest run has stats.phase / done / total while running.
GET http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/runs?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5b. One run (status: running | completed | partial | failed, plus fileErrors)
GET http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/runs/REPLACE_RUN_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Repositories in this bot, with file / unit / relationship counts
GET http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/repos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Delete one repository (its code, relationships and embeddings). 409 while a run is in progress.
DELETE http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/repos/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### (Phases 6-7 endpoints are documented below.)

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Retrieval and chat (Phase 6-7)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8. Retrieval only — what the model would be shown, without asking it.
###    Useful for checking why an answer was wrong: was it the search or the model?
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/search
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "query": "what happens when the users page loads",
    "limit": 12
}

### 9. Ask a question. mode "answer" (default) retrieves once then answers;
###    mode "agent" lets the model call the tools below itself (slower, better
###    for multi-step questions). Returns { answer, citations, queryType }.
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "question": "where are all users loaded from the database?",
    "mode": "answer"
}

### 10. Agent mode
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "question": "trace what happens when the users page loads",
    "mode": "agent"
}

### 11. Tools, callable directly (the same handlers the agent loop uses):
###     search_code, find_symbol, get_unit, read_file, get_callers, get_callees,
###     list_routes, trace_feature, get_summary
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/tools/list_routes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{}

### 11b. Follow a feature end to end (uid comes from find_symbol or search_code)
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/tools/trace_feature
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "uid": "shop:src/pages/UsersPage.tsx#UsersPage"
}

### 11c. Find a symbol by name
POST http://localhost:3000/code/{{botId}}/tools/find_symbol
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "name": "findAll"
}

### Evaluate retrieval quality (CLI, not HTTP):
###   npm run code:eval -- --bot <botId>
### Reports recall@5, recall@10 and MRR against eval/questions.json.
